    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39066": {
      "title": "Job Details",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Instructor 12 Mo Working Title Teaching Assistant or Associate Professor of Large Animal Ambulatory Practice Position # F00730 Department College of Veterinary Medicine Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/15/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a faculty position in Large Animal Veterinary Ambulatory Medicine and Surgery (Equine and Livestock). This will be a 12-month, full time, non-tenure track, Assistant or Associate Professor position. Rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. This will be a predominantly clinical position (60-80% clinical service and clinical teaching), pre-clinical (years 1-3) teaching (10-30%), and service (10%). Promoting and providing large animal ambulatory veterinary services to the Jonesboro and surrounding local communities. Duties & Responsibilities: Promote the A-State Large Animal Ambulatory Service Provide day-time veterinary ambulatory care to large animal species including horses, donkeys, cattle, sheep, goats, and swine to the Jonesboro community, surrounding  communities, and any other stakeholders (8-a.m. to 5-p.m.)  (estimated 50% livestock and 50% equine patients) Provide emergency veterinary ambulatory care to established A-State Large Animal Ambulatory Veterinary service clients and A-State animals Lead and manage herd-health protocols for established ambulatory clients Work collaboratively with other A-State and local veterinarians and staff Manage ambulatory technician personnel Contribute to didactic and clinicals skills related education for DVM students Contribute to large animal IACUC protocols. Contribute to college and university committees and/or serve on regional or national professional organizations Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: • Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and staff • Ability to communicate effectively across CVM stakeholders • Ability to prioritize tasks, deliver results in a timely manner, and function independently General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. On-call afterhours care as needed to established clients and A-State animals Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date The search will continue until the position is filled. Those who apply by the closing date will receive priority consideration. Required documents: Cover letter, curriculum vitae, and names and contact information of three references Minimum Qualifications: • DVM or equivalent • Board certification in a large-animal specialty (e.g., ACVS-LA, ACVIM-LA) (preferred) E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39744": {
      "title": "Job Details",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Temporary Instructor 9 Mo Working Title Temporary Instructor in Biotechnology Position # F00647 Department Biological Sciences Apply Now Employment Status: Temporary (1 Year Assignment) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/14/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Biological Sciences, housed in the Beck College of Science and Mathematics, is seeking a full-time Temporary Instructor to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in biotechnology and molecular biology for the Spring 2027 semester (January 1 – May 15, 2026). Continued employment beyond the initial appointment may be possible, subject to funding availability and successful performance. The successful candidate will contribute to the education and professional preparation of undergraduate and graduate students through a combination of advanced scientific knowledge, laboratory-based instruction, and application of current biotechnology methods and technologies. The program features a well-equipped biotechnology teaching laboratory and with additional access to select core instrumentation and resources within the Arkansas Biosciences Institute, the university's biotech research facility. Duties & Responsibilities: The successful candidate will join a collaborative team of interdisciplinary biotechnology and cell/molecular faculty group who are committed to supporting new instructors as they transition into both the classroom and laboratory environment. Experienced faculty members will serve as teaching resources and mentors to facilitate a successful onboarding experience. The instructor will be responsible for teaching the following courses: Molecular Biology (graduate and undergraduate sections): Instruction will focus on both foundational and advanced concepts in molecular biology, with an emphasis on their applications in biotechnology. Lab in Biotechniques II (graduate and undergraduate sections): An advanced laboratory course that emphasizes hands-on application of molecular and cellular biotechnology techniques. Course content may incorporate the instructor’s areas of expertise and research interests. Applications of Biotechnology: The undergraduate Biotechnology Program's capstone course. The instructor will guide students in professional development activities and supervise the completion of a capstone project. While instructors have flexibility in shaping course content, the curriculum is well-established, and teaching materials, including lecture presentations, assignments, and other resources, are available to support course delivery. Preferred Expertise Candidates should demonstrate a strong foundation in molecular and cellular biology and the ability to apply these principles in biotechnology. Preferred qualifications include experience in one or more of the following areas: Expertise in several relevant wet-laboratory methods, experimental design, and data analysis. Biotechnology laboratory techniques and applications including DNA/RNA analysis, gene expression, and related molecular methods. Cell culture and cellular technologies. Bioinformatics and computational approaches in biotechnology. Integration of molecular and cellular biology concepts with modern biotechnology applications. Consideration will be given to candidates who can incorporate bioinformatics and contemporary biotechnology approaches into classroom and laboratory instruction. Preferred Qualifications: College or university teaching experience. Experience teaching laboratory-based biotechnology or molecular biology courses. Expertise in bioinformatics or computational biology. Industry, research, or applied biotechnology experience. Familiarity with capstone structured courses (taking them and/or teaching). Responsibilities Develop and deliver engaging undergraduate and graduate-level instruction. Provide hands-on laboratory instruction and demonstrate current molecular and biotechnology techniques. Integrate real-world applications, current research, and industry practices into coursework. Teach and assess student learning through assignments, laboratory activities, projects, examinations, and other appropriate methods. Mentor students and support their development of professional biotechnology skills. Communicate about current advances in molecular biology, biotechnology, cellular technologies, and bioinformatics. Contribute to the academic and professional goals of the Biotechnology Program. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Strong background in molecular biology and biotechnology. Demonstrated hands-on experience with molecular and/or cellular laboratory techniques. Ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and/or graduate level General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Biotechnology, Molecular Biology, Cell Biology, Biochemistry, Biology, or a closely related field. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39713": {
      "title": "Job Details",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Temporary Instructor 9 Mo Working Title Temporary Instructor of Nursing Position # F00303 Department School of Nursing Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Telecommute - Jonesboro Campus Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/12/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Nine (9) month undergraduate nontenure-track faculty position in the ACEN accredited A-State School of Nursing. Participation in teaching, student advising, professional service is expected; scholarly activity desired. This position is full-time at the rank of instructor. Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching Faculty: Accepts delegated appropriate assignments and responsibilities Accepts responsibility for assessing student learning and evaluating student learning outcomes Teaching: Actively participates in development, revision, and evaluation of curriculum, course content, clinical experiences, and test construction Is responsible for didactic courses and/or clinical group size appropriate to area of clinical practice Plans and supervises clinical seminars Establishes effective coordinating relationships with co-workers and clinical agencies Continues education for professional growth Service: Participates in academic advising and guidance of students Maintains office hours as required by the college Participates in the faculty organization and appropriate program, college and university activities Sponsors and promotes planned activities of students, program, college and university as requested Contributes to the community through involvement in and/or consultation to health related organizations, board memberships, or professional presentations to the public Participates in planning for the continued growth and progress of the program through faculty and student recruitment and retention efforts Holds membership and participates in organizations that advance the profession of nursing and advanced practice nursing, such as the ANA or other professional organizations Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of curriculum design, strategies to promote student learning, assessment and evaluation of learning, evidence-based education principles, basic nursing skills and a commitment to life-long learning Possess interpersonal and communication skills necessary to teach as part of a faculty team General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday Hours vary depending on teaching and/or clinical rotation assignments; faculty organization; and appropriate program, college and university activities. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date 15-credit-hour teaching workload Academic experience preferred A cover letter, resume, and reference list must be attached (in MS Word or PDF format) to page four of the electronic application This position has been identified as a telecommuting position. The duties are performed during standard work hours of 8am-5pm at a predefined and approved work location. Individuals filling this role must have a dedicated workspace that provides privacy and security related to the work being performed. Additionally, individuals must have secure internet access with appropriate upload/download capabilities to perform the duties associated with the position. Individuals in this position will be required to review and acknowledge the Telecommuting Guidelines and Telecommuting Agreement for A-State Location Requirement:  To be considered for this position, candidates must reside in Arkansas or a state that shares a border with Arkansas (Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee, Missouri, or Oklahoma.  This residency requirement supports team collaboration, regional knowledge, and occasional in-person engagement as needed. Preferred Qualifications: Online Teaching Experience Minimum Qualifications: An earned Master of Science in Nursing Degree is required. Two (2) years of clinical practice as a RN Must be eligible for licensure to practice nursing in Arkansas Teaching experience required E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39726": {
      "title": "Job Details",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Fiscal Support Manager Working Title Treasury Services Specialist Position # A01311 Department Assoc VC for Finance/CTO Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/14/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Fiscal Support Manager is responsible for overseeing the operations of various fiscal division programs by establishing work priorities and standards of performance, and supervising staff. This position is governed by Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP), state and federal laws, and institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Preparation and submission of non-student accounts receivable invoices Reconciliation of non-student accounts receivable balances, including aging reports and analysis Prepare daily incoming check log for cashiering operations Assist the Director of Treasury Services with month end journal entries and reporting Manage departmental ordering and budget monitoring; serves as the office’s financial lead Assist with student inquiries via email, telephone, and in person during peak seasons Process credit card returns Process deposit releases Serve as the backup for various daily tasks including bank transactions, assist in the preparation of reports and documentation used for monthly bank reconciliations Assist with reporting and analysis of student data as requested by the Treasurer, Director of Student Financial Services, and/or Director of Treasury Conduct additional financial analysis in support of the office’s efficient and effective operation Work with the Director of Treasury Services to complete year end journal entries and reporting Develop dashboards and other analytical solutions to support operations Monthly reconciliation of assigned accounts Serve as the departmental lead for continuous review and update of standard operating procedures Possess excellent verbal and written communication skills, as well as customer service skills Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of database accounting and management principles, applicable laws and regulations of assigned section, computers and software application programs, and customer service techniques Proficient in Microsoft Office such as Excel and Word Ability to record fiscal data and manipulate data to generate complex reports and documents and conduct research and perform basic quantitative quality assurance reviews General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a Bachelor's Degree in accounting, finance, or a business related field. Two (2) years of bookkeeping, basic accounting, billing, or related experience. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements upon approval of the qualifications review committee. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39785": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Administrative Specialist III Working Title Administrative Specialist III Position # A01019 Department Financial Aid and Scholarships Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $30,000.00 Closing: 9/21/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Administrative Specialist III is responsible for researching and preparing special reports, examining and verifying documents, and performing general office duties. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy Duties & Responsibilities: Provides assistance and other resources to potential and current students, parents, staff, faculty and off-campus agencies Input documents into the administrative information system Manage Title IV Loans, Federal PLUS Loans, and Private Loan programs and Hard-Copy checks Assist with various projects Oversee the exit interview process Participate in testing the administrative information system Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of record-keeping procedures, the principles and practices of mathematics and statistics, work-related subject area, and computers and software applications. Ability to conduct research and compile data into report form, establish and maintain filing systems, operate standard office equipment, analyze documents to determine compliance with rules, regulations, and procedures, and communicate both orally and in writing. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assists Students, Parents, Staff, Faculty, and Student loan Guarantee foundations, and Lenders Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a High School Diploma One (1) years of experience in a specialized or related area applicable to work performed E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
