    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39741": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Dance and Choreography 9 Mo Position # F00266 Department Theatre Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/9/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Theatre at Arkansas State University invites applications for a Full-Time Assistant Professor of Theatre in Dance and Choreography. This is a 9-month tenure-track teaching appointment starting Fall 2027. Duties & Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be responsible for: Teaching a 4/4 load, which typically includes three academic courses and one production course (directing/choreographing). Other possible courses include, but are not limited to, Theatre Appreciation, Ballet, Musical Theatre Dance, Jazz Dance, Tap Dance, Folk and other Dance courses as determined by the faculty member’s area(s) of specialty and expertise. Maintaining an active record of research and/or creative activity Overseeing the Stage Manager for shows when directing. Attending evening/weekend rehearsals as appropriate Mentoring and supervising student choreographers and dance captains. Being available for student supervision during evening and weekend rehearsals and performances Working collegially and collaboratively with students and faculty. Department Overview: The Arkansas State University Department of Theatre offers rigorous theatre training in a liberal arts environment. Students receive a comprehensive education, whether choosing a general approach or the more select experiences within the three emphases: Acting, Design and Technology, or Musical Theatre. The curriculum is designed to combine classroom instruction with practical production experience, as both are integral to the student’s development. Classroom experiences provide theoretical, historical, and critical examinations of the theatre as art, craft, and discipline, while production experiences offer practical opportunities for exploring and applying these concepts. This liberal arts-based education provides opportunities to master critical thinking, communication, and creative problem-solving skills, preparing graduates to become engaged, thoughtful, and compassionate citizens of a global world. Facilities: The Department of Theatre is housed within Fowler Center, Arkansas State University’s premier performing arts complex. The 344-seat Drama Theatre serves as the primary venue for plays and musicals, featuring stepped seating to maximize sight lines and acoustics designed for spoken drama productions. The proscenium features a 40’ x 20’ opening, and a complete catwalk system provides access for lighting and rigging areas. The stage house features a suspended floor and full fly-loft, rigged so that scenic properties may be “flown” out of view. Adjacent to the Drama Theatre is the Simpson Theatre, a flexible black box space that allows for various configurations, providing students opportunities to develop skills required to work in many different kinds of venues. Additional facilities include a Light Lab equipped with intelligent LED theatrical lighting and a small theatrical sound system, a Design Lab featuring Apple iMacs with CAD, lighting and sound design software, and access to Adobe’s Creative Cloud, as well as drafting tables and a wide-format printer. The Costume Shop is equipped with 14 Bernina sewing machines, industrial irons, sergers, a dye vat, cutting tables, and an embroidery machine. The Scene Shop is among the finest in the region, equipped with a variety of professional-grade stationary and portable power tools, as well as a 3D printer. About Arkansas State University: Arkansas State University (A-State), founded in 1909, is the second largest university in Arkansas and serves over 15,000 students. As a Carnegie Research 2 institution and the premier university of the mid-South, A-State is committed to teaching, research, and service. Located in Jonesboro, A-State offers a vibrant campus life with a diverse student body and a strong tradition of student-focused instruction. With more than 150 degree programs, including robust online offerings, A-State combines world-class research with academic excellence and is a catalyst for progress in the Delta and Mid-South region. About Jonesboro: Jonesboro is the regional hub of Northeast Arkansas for healthcare, entertainment, business and industry. It is the 5th largest city in Arkansas with a population of over 76,000. The Metropolitan Statistical Area (MSA) encompasses over 130,000 people. The A\u0002State campus is centrally located in Jonesboro with the thriving downtown entertainment sector to the west and the growing Hilltop area to the east. Jonesboro provides convenient access to major markets via interstate and four-lane highways. Memphis, TN (1 hour), Little Rock, AR (2 hours), St. Louis, MO (4 hours), and Nashville, TN (4 hours). Additional Considerations: Experience directing theatrical productions. Experience teaching Theatre for non-majors. Experience teaching ballet or other foundational dance techniques. Membership in professional organizations such as SETC, ACDA, or MTEA. Other Teaching Areas of Expertise: Stage Combat, Movement for Actors, Yoga, Non-Western Dance Techniques Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Applicant should present evidence of excellence in teaching, active scholarly and creative work, knowledge of current trends in the field, and artistic leadership in the areas of theatrical dance and choreography. General Days/Hours: Monday through Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM plus additional hours for production(s) on weekdays, weekends and evenings. Other: Application deadline: Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applications for position F00266 must be received online. This position is housed on the Jonesboro campus. Visit https://jobs.astate.edu for detailed information and to apply for the position. Please upload the following: ▪ Cover letter addressing qualifications ▪ Curriculum vitae ▪ Indication of professional dance and/or choreography work, such as a portfolio, performance reel, or documentation of creative work. ▪ Contact information for five professional references Transcripts will be requested by the search committee after initial screening of applicants. For additional information, please contact: DayDay Robinson, Assistant Professor of Theatre. Email: drobinson@astate.edu Minimum Qualifications: ▪ M.F.A. in Theatre, Dance, or a closely related field, or equivalent professional experience. ▪ Demonstrated proficiency in teaching both dance and choreography for theatrical productions. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39759": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Political Science Position # F00286 Department Government-Law-Policy Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/19/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Government, Law & Policy at Arkansas State University, a Carnegie-classified R2 research university, invites applications for a tenure-track position at the level of assistant professor, beginning in Fall 2027. The search is open with respect to subfield and substantive focus within political science. We seek a colleague with an active, publishable research agenda who will contribute to the department's growing research profile and its graduate programs (an MA in Political Science and a NASPAA-accredited MPA). Because our curricular needs span the discipline, we are especially interested in candidates prepared to teach across more than one area, including political institutions, state and local government, international relations, and research methods. The teaching load is consistent with the department's research expectations. Duties & Responsibilities: The teaching load is consistent with those at research-oriented institutions and with the department’s expectations for research productivity. Faculty workload includes research, service, and professional development in the best interest of the students and community at large. Faculty members deliver instruction, carry out research, perform service for their respective professions and community, and participate in the management of the University through shared governance. Each member of the faculty has the duty to deliver instruction and maintain a learning environment consistent with the highest standards of the profession. The faculty has a responsibility to set degree requirements, assess when they are met, and establish and maintain curricula that meet professional standards and fulfill the educational goals of the University. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge, skills, and abilities required or applicable to the position responsibilities and area of specialization, including special abilities. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date All items listed below are requirements must be submitted in order for your file to be considered complete: (1) A statement of purpose indicating research and teaching interests (2) Curriculum Vitae (3) a writing sample (e.g., recent peer-reviewed article, book chapter, or dissertation chapter) (4) three letters of recommendation Arkansas State University is a comprehensive public research university located approximately 70 miles northwest of Memphis, TN. The department offers a well-rounded curriculum to its more than 100 majors. The department also offers two graduate programs—an MA in Political Science and a NASPAA-accredited MPA program. The latter includes an enrollment of more than 150 students Questions can be directed to cwimpy@astate.edu Minimum Qualifications: PhD in political science or a cognate field. ABD candidates will be considered, but the doctorate must be completed by the start date of the appointment. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39792": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Public Administration Position # F00192 Department Government-Law-Policy Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/19/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Government, Law & Policy at Arkansas State University, a Carnegie-classified R2 research university, invites applications for a tenure-track position at the level of assistant professor in public administration, beginning in Fall 2027. The search is open with respect to area of specialization within public administration and public policy, and comparative perspectives are welcome. We seek a colleague with an active, publishable research agenda who will contribute to the department's growing research profile and to its NASPAA-accredited MPA program, where the primary teaching responsibility will lie. Because our curricular needs in the MPA program span the field, we are especially interested in candidates prepared to teach across more than one area, including some combination of public management, leadership, grant writing, and human resources management. The successful candidate will also occasionally contribute to the department's undergraduate offerings in political science. The teaching load is consistent with the department's research expectations. Duties & Responsibilities: The teaching load of the faculty is in alignment with a Carnegie-classified R2 research institution. Faculty workload includes research, service, and professional development in the best interest of the students and community at large. Faculty members deliver instruction, carry out research, perform service for their respective professions and community, and participate in the management of the University through shared governance. Each member of the faculty has the duty to deliver instruction and maintain a learning environment consistent with the highest standards of the profession. The faculty has a responsibility to set degree requirements, assess when they are met, and establish and maintain curricula that meet professional standards and fulfill the educational goals of the University. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge, skills, and abilities required or applicable to the position responsibilities and area of specialization, including special abilities. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date All items listed below are required and must be submitted in order for your file to be considered complete: (1) A statement of purpose indicating research and teaching interests (2) Curriculum Vitae (3) A writing sample (e.g., recent peer-reviewed article, book chapter, or dissertation chapter) (4) Three letters of recommendation, to be requested if selected for interview. Arkansas State University is a comprehensive public research university located approximately 70 miles northwest of Memphis, TN. The department offers a well-rounded curriculum to its more than 120 majors. The department also offers two graduate programs—an MA in Political Science and a NASPAA-accredited MPA program, the latter with an enrollment of more than 230 students. Questions can be directed to cwimpy@astate.edu Minimum Qualifications: PhD in public administration, public policy, political science, or a cognate field. ABD candidates will be considered, but the doctorate must be completed by the start date of the appointment. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
