    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39783": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Project Program Specialist Working Title Financial Aid Coordinator Position # A00078 Department Financial Aid and Scholarships Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/21/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Loan and Data Load Coordinator administers federal student loan programs while ensuring compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations. This position is responsible for loan origination, disbursement, reconciliation, Return to Title IV (R2T4) calculations, overaward resolution, system data processing, and student eligibility review. The coordinator serves as a subject matter expert for student loan programs and supports students, families, faculty, and staff through professional customer service and financial aid counseling. Additionally, this position will supervise the processing team. The position works collaboratively with Financial Aid and Scholarships staff, Enrollment Management and Finance departments to ensure accurate and timely delivery of financial assistance. Duties & Responsibilities: Federal Loan Administration Administer Federal Direct Loan programs (subsidized and unsubsidized loans) which include reviewing and processing loan increases, decreases, cancellations, and reinstatements. Originate, adjust, disburse, and cancel student loans in compliance with federal regulations and institutional policies. System Processing and Data Management Review rejected records and resolve processing exceptions. Maintain accurate electronic records and documentation. Review and resolve suspended institutional student information records (ISIRs) to verify demographic information is correct prior to awarding federal aid to students. Compliance and Eligibility Review Conduct reviews for overawards, unmet need, and cost-of-attendance conflicts. Ensure compliance with Title IV regulations, federal guidance, institutional policies, and audit requirements. Reconciliation and Reporting Perform Direct Loan reconciliation between Banner and federal systems. Collaborate with the Treasurer’s Office to process unclaimed refunds checks to return funds to Federal Student Aid. Return to Title IV (R2T4) Administration Calculate and process Return to Title IV funds for students who withdraw. Ensure required adjustments and notifications are completed accurately and timely. Student Service and Counseling Respond to inquiries via phone, email, and in-person appointments. Assist students with FAFSA-related issues and aid processing requirements. Maintain student confidentiality in accordance with FERPA. Supervising the Processing Team Oversee the Processing Team functions, such as Pell Grant, Direct Plus Loan, and Private Loan processing and reconciliation. Monitor adherence to federal, state and institutional regulations Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of supervisory practices and procedures, student financial aid programs, standards, and procedures. Ability to review and evaluate student financial needs, and prepare appropriate financial aid packages, disseminate information orally and in writing. Collect, analyze, compile, and record data on financial aid, and supervise the work of subordinates. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Preferred Qualifications - One (1) year of experience in student financial aid or other related areas. Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of an earned Bachelor's degree. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or parts of these basic requirements upon the approval of the qualifications review committee. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39756": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Project Program Specialist Working Title International Tax and Collections Manager Position # A00363 Department Assoc VC for Finance/CTO Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $50,000 - $53,000 Closing: 9/16/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The International Tax and Collections Manager reports to the Director of Student Financial Services in the Treasurer’s Office and is responsible for establishing sound business practices and internal controls within the area of student accounts receivable and collections. The International Tax and Collections Manager acts as the primary liaison between the Treasurer’s Office and the collection agencies, as well as working with students and supervising staff. Duties & Responsibilities: Responsible for establishing tax files for eligible international students, faculty, staff and vendors Calculate taxable amounts for various scholarships and generate, as well as file, 1042 and 1042S forms Stay abreast of all international tax laws and ensure the University is in compliance Maintain student, faculty, staff and vendor records within Glacier software Responsible for managing overall student and employee account collections Establish and monitor business practices and customer service processes within the collections area Works with collection agency representatives to manage ongoing collection efforts Submits outstanding collections to the State of Arkansas state income tax refund set-off program for potential recoveries Oversee the billing, collecting, and reconciling of all Perkins loan accounts Primary contact to build stores and products within the e-commerce site Marketplace Assists and counsels students as needed by phone or in person with account questions, payment plans, and other information Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of business and financial practices and internal controls. Excellent communication and customer service skills. Ability to organize and prioritize multiple tasks and projects General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Inform/advise the Chief Financial Officer, the Associate VC for Finance, and the Director of Student Financial Services on all matters of a financial, business, or administrative nature Minimum Qualifications: An earned Bachelor’s Degree in Accounting, Finance, or other business related field E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39749": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Instructor 9 Month Working Title Online Instructor of Public Administration Position # F00582 Department Government-Law-Policy Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Telecommute - Jonesboro Campus Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/19/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Government, Law & Policy at Arkansas State University, a Carnegie-classified R2 research university, invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position in public administration, beginning in Fall 2027. This is a fully online teaching position, and the successful candidate may work remotely. The primary teaching responsibility will be in the department's NASPAA-accredited online MPA program, with the potential to also teach public administration and policy courses in the department's online undergraduate program in political science. The search is open with respect to area of specialization within public administration and public policy. Because our online curricular needs span the field, we are especially interested in candidates with flexible teaching interests who are prepared to teach across more than one area, including some combination of public management, leadership, budgeting and finance, grant writing, human resources management, and non-profit management. Candidates with substantial applied experience in public or nonprofit organizations are encouraged to apply, as are candidates with a demonstrated record of effective online instruction. Duties & Responsibilities: The primary responsibility of this position is the delivery of high-quality online instruction in the MPA program and, as needed, the online undergraduate program in political science. Although all faculty are expected to mentor students, the primary focus of this position is teaching courses and contributing to the ongoing success of the MPA program. Other duties as assigned. All items listed below are required and must be submitted in order for your file to be considered complete : A statement of purpose indicating teaching interests and relevant professional experience Curriculum Vitae Evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., sample syllabi, student evaluations, or a brief teaching statement addressing online instruction) Three letters of recommendation, to be requested if selected for interview. Arkansas State University is a comprehensive public research university located approximately 70 miles northwest of Memphis, TN. The department offers a well-rounded curriculum to its more than 120 majors. The department also offers two graduate programs—an MA in Political Science and a NASPAA-accredited MPA program, the latter with an enrollment of more than 230 students. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge, skills, and abilities required or applicable to the position responsibilities and area of specialization, including special abilities. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date This position has been identified as a telecommuting position. The duties are performed during standard work hours of 8am-5pm at a predefined and approved work location. Individuals filling this role must have dedicated workspace that provides privacy and security related to the work being performed. Additionally, individuals must have secure internet access with appropriate upload/download capabilities to perform the duties associated with the position. Individuals in this position will be required to review and acknowledge the Telecommuting Guidelines and Telecommuting Agreement for A-State. Location Requirement: To be considered for this position, candidates must reside in Arkansas or a state that shares a border with Arkansas (Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee, Missouri, or Oklahoma. This residency requirement supports team collaboration, regional knowledge, and occasional in-person engagement as needed. The primarily online teaching modality means that some flexibility may be needed in work schedules to accommodate student needs. Applicants wishing to work in person will be provided with a full faculty office and resources should that be preferred. Questions can be sent to cwimpy@astate.edu Minimum Qualifications: An earned MPA or a related master's degree with substantial professional experience in public or nonprofit management is required. PhD, DPA, or other terminal degree in public administration, public policy, political science, or a cognate field is preferred. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39784": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Project Program Specialist Working Title Program Coordinator/Athletics Financial Aid Coordinator Position # A00263 Department Financial Aid and Scholarships Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/21/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Program Coordinator is responsible for one or more academic or social programs at an institution of higher education. This position is governed by state and federal laws and institutional policy. This position reports to the Associate Director of Scholarships. Duties & Responsibilities: Work directly with the Associate Director of Scholarships in support of Athletic Operations, which includes effectively providing sports information guidance for the institution's NCAA Division program, in accordance with university, conference, and NCAA rules and regulations. Coordinate the awarding of NCAA student-athlete scholarships in conjunction with Athletics. Provide assistance and information for financial aid through processing applications, budgeting, packaging, adjusting financial aid per federal and state requirements, verifying data, answering phones, greeting visitors, interpreting and explaining federal and state regulations, policies, and procedures. Management of completed counselor’s list of students to be awarded financial aid on a daily basis. Assist students in the completion of financial aid applications and verification forms, review documentation, and determine applicant status. Counsel students and provide accurate information concerning all financial aid opportunities for federal, state, and institutional financial aid. Compose routine correspondence, type and process various lists and forms on a daily basis. Coordinate with and travel to A-State Degree Centers, two-year colleges, and high schools to present information and offer presentations to a variety of populations, including students, parents, faculty, and staff. Presentations will consist of all areas of financial aid as well as collaboration with Transfer Coaches on recruitment events. Quarterly travel may be required to each A-State Degree Center. Occasional travel will be required to attend professional development workshops as well as federal, regional, and state conferences, particularly regarding NCAA compliance regulations. Compile and maintain on a daily basis a variety of statistical information related to financial aid from the advisor master list that is produced each day. · A-State uses Banner/Ellucian as its student information system. The successful candidate will become proficient in navigating the system to ensure students are awarded properly and according to federal, state, and university guidelines. Demonstrate a sense of collaboration and communication with the public, other departments, and outside agencies, and work within a team to provide financial aid information to our students. Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of the organization and administration of various higher education academic and social programs Knowledge of campus and community resources Knowledge of state, federal, and campus rules, regulations, and requirements related to campus academic and social programs Ability to coordinate the activities of campus academic and/or social programs Ability to evaluate collected information and formulate into recommendations Ability to compile information into report form General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Must be able to: • Learn the Financial Aid Application Procedure • Maintain accurate and complete records for students • Communicate effectively both orally and in writing • Establish and maintain effective communication with others • Be able to multitask; meet schedules and timelines • Work confidentially with discretion • Answer telephones Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of an earned Bachelor's Degree Other job related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements upon approval of the qualifications review committee E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39813": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Student Account Specialist Working Title Student Account Specialist Position # A01125 Department Assoc VC for Finance/CTO Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/19/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Student Accounts Specialist is responsible for processing student financial accounts at an institution of higher education. This position is governed by state and federal laws and institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Assist students with account questions and provide guidance Answers and disseminates departmental telephone calls Composes, types, and edits various documents and/or jobs Meets and directs visitors to appropriate areas Processes incoming student/departmental forms and enters necessary information to file or start proper process flow Processes incoming return mail by entering appropriate information and then filing according to standards Reviews and disseminates departmental faxes Collects daily departmental mail, shredding, and scanning Reviews bad address reports and enters information as necessary Completes and mails return check notifications Receives and reviews scanned departmental documents Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of student financial aid programs. Knowledge of collection procedures and methods Ability to participate in student account activities. Ability to compile and report information and statistics from student accounts Ability to explain policies and regulations to students concerning accounts General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a High School Diploma Two (2) years of experience in a specialized or related area applicable to work performed. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=38795": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 12 Mo Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Small Animal Urgent Care Position # F00722 Department College of Veterinary Medicine Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/29/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a clinical assistant or associate professor in Small Animal Urgent Care. Rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. This position incorporates clinical work (24 weeks/year) with workplace-based year 4 student training in urgent care/emergency, teaching of year 1-3 students in clinical skills and urgent/emergency care. Service (10%) is also expected. Scholarly activity appointment is negotiable. Duties & Responsibilities: Teach year 1-3 DVM students the principles and practice of urgent care and emergency medicine in the classroom, clinical skills laboratory Teach year 4 DVM students urgent care and emergency medicine in clinical practice Provide excellent patient care and clinical service, including communication with clients and referring veterinarians Contribute to competency-based curriculum development with a focus on small animal emergency medicine and urgent care across years 1-4 of the DVM curriculum Contribute to objective structured clinical examinations (OSCEs) and other skills-based assessments Contribute to college and university committees and/or serve on regional or national professional organizations Mentor and advise DVM students +/- Contribute to scholarly endeavors through collaborative educational research and/or educational innovations Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: • Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and staff. • Ability to communicate effectively across CVM stakeholders. • Ability to prioritize tasks, deliver results in a timely manner, and function independently. General Days/Hours: Variable hours (approximately 4 pm-12 am when on clinical duty, M-Th, ~24 weeks per year; 8 am-5 pm M-F when not on clinic duty) Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date The search will continue until the position is filled. Those who apply by the closing date will receive priority consideration. Required Documents: Cover letter, curriculum vitae, and names and contact information of three references Minimum Qualifications: • DVM or equivalent • Board certification in a small animal specialty (preferred) (e.g., ACVECC) • Two (2) years of teaching experience (preferred) • Experience in competency-based veterinary education (preferred) E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=38557": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Faculty 12 Mo Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Small Animal Practice Position # F00486 Department College of Veterinary Medicine Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/29/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a faculty position in Small Animal Practice. This will be a 12-month, full time, non-tenure track, Assistant or Associate Professor position. Rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. This will be a predominantly teaching position (85% teaching) and include research/scholarly activities and service. Teaching of DVM students will be in a competency-based veterinary curriculum incorporating lecture, lab and small group learning. Duties & Responsibilities: Teach small animal clinical and surgical skills and communication and professionalism to DVM students using models, simulations, specimens, and live animals in years 1-4, in laboratory sessions, small and large group classroom sessions Work with other clinical and professional skills veterinarians and staff Contribute to competency-based curriculum development with a focus on small animal professional, clinical and surgical skills across years 1-4 of the DVM curriculum Contribute to development of assessments in communication, professionalism, and clinical skills, including objective structured clinical examinations (OSCEs) Contribute to college and university committees and/or serve on regional or national professional organizations Contribute to scholarly endeavors through collaborative educational research and/or educational innovations Contribute to classroom instruction of DVM students (large and small group) Responsibilities may include clinical practice if desired Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and staff Ability to communicate effectively across CVM stakeholders Ability to prioritize tasks, deliver results in a timely manner and function independently General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note that all position postings close at 12:00 am CST on the position closing date. The search will continue until the position is filled. Those who apply by the closing date will receive priority consideration. Preferred Qualifications: • Two years of teaching experience (preferred) • Experience in competency-based veterinary education (preferred) Required Documents • Cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, and names and contact information of three references Minimum Qualifications: An earned Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) or equivalent is required for this position. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39834": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Administrative Specialist III Working Title Administrative Specialist III Position # A00983 Department Dean of Education-Behavioral Sci Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $30,000.00 Closing: 9/28/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Administrative Specialist III coordinates office operations, researches and prepares specialized reports, and assists in the development, implementation, and revision of administrative policies and procedures under the direction of the supervisor. This position operates in compliance with applicable state and federal regulations, as well as agency and institutional policies. This position will cover the Department of Educational Leadership, Doctoral Program, and Teacher Education. Duties & Responsibilities: Maintain calendar, tracking, and office databases. Maintains department files. Handles all the student traffic and day-to-day operations of office duties assigned. Provides fiscal support for the departments. This includes, but is not limited to, ordering and receiving goods, reconciling the department’s P-Card with the budget, preparing budget statements, working with the grants office, ESFs, Taleo offers, EPAFs, travel for faculty, extra compensation forms, and GA staffing. Provides technical assistance, guidance, and information to internal and external stakeholders, vendors, and other customers by researching and interpreting federal and state laws and agency policies and procedures. Enter information/projects into university computer systems, such as Banner, Concur, Knowledge Base, etc. Serve as the travel delegate for the faculty Reviews operating departmental budgets and financial policies and procedures Monitors department budgets, reviews and approves expenditures, advises management of potential budget issues, and makes budget recommendations. Ensures the accuracy of financial data and produces financial and statistical reports for the assigned departments. Gathers technical information for monthly reports and studies and presents to the appropriate authorities. Performs other duties as assigned. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of business and management principles involved in strategic planning, resource allocation, and human resources. Knowledge of the principles and practices of fiscal management, including budget development, purchasing, and asset management. Knowledge of the principles and practices of mathematics and statistics, research and analysis techniques and methods, work-related subject area, and computers and software applications. Knowledge of state and federal laws, rules, and regulations, and agency/institution policies and applicable laws. Ability to prepare budgets and monitor expenditures. Ability to prepare and present oral and written information and reports. Ability to interpret and apply laws, policies, and procedures. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM Regular and reliable attendance Additional hours as requested/needed Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Preferred Qualifications: - The formal education equivalent of an earned Bachelor's Degree in general business, finance, or a related field - Accounting knowledge preferred Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a High School Diploma One (1) year of specialized training in office management, business, or a related field Two (2) years of experience in a specialized or a related field applicable to work performed E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39832": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Project Program Specialist Working Title Assistant Director of Human Resources Position # A00506 Department Human Resources Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/23/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Assistant Director of Human Resources supports the administration of Arkansas State University human resources programs, policies, and procedures. The position provides guidance and assistance to employees, supervisors, faculty, and administrators regarding employee relations, leave administration, reasonable accommodations, immigration compliance, performance management, and other employment-related matters. The Assistant Director works closely with the Director of Human Resources and University departments to promote consistent policy application and compliance with applicable federal and state laws. The Assistant Director will supervise 5+ employees within the Human Resources Department. Duties & Responsibilities: Provides guidance and support regarding employee relations matters, including performance concerns, workplace complaints, disciplinary actions, and other employment-related issues. Assists with employee relations investigations, disciplinary and termination meetings; maintains appropriate confidential documentation. Maintains immigration compliance by monitoring Public Access Files and employment authorization status and ensuring required documentation is maintained. Serves as a liaison between the University, employees, departments, and the University's immigration attorney regarding employment-based immigration matters. Assists with H-1B Visa, O-1 Visa, permanent residency, and other employment-based immigration processes. Interprets and applies University policies and applicable federal and state employment laws and regulations. Assists with the development, review, and implementation of HR policies, procedures, forms, and training. Provides HR guidance and training to supervisors, employees, faculty, and administrators. Maintains confidential personnel and human resources records and prepares reports and correspondence as needed. Collaborates with Payroll, Benefits, Academic Affairs, and other University offices on HR-related matters. Assists the Director of Human Resources with special projects, compliance initiatives, and other HR programs. Performs other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: · Knowledge of human resources principles, practices, and applicable employment laws and regulations. · Knowledge of employee relations, FMLA, ADA, immigration compliance, and employment practices. · Ability to interpret and apply policies and regulations appropriately and consistently. · Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. · Ability to handle sensitive and confidential matters with discretion and professionalism. · Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. · Ability to exercise sound judgment, resolve problems, and work effectively with employees at all levels of the University. · Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet established deadlines. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM Regular and reliable attendance Additional hours as needed Other: Preferred Qualifications · Experience in higher education or a public-sector environment. · Experience with employee relations, FMLA/ADA administration, workplace investigations, and employment-based immigration compliance. Minimum Qualifications: · Bachelor’s degree in human resources, Business Administration, Management, or a related field. · Three years of progressively responsible human resources experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. · Experience in handling confidential employee and employment-related matters E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39831": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Skilled Tradesman Working Title Skilled Tradesman Position # A00674 Department Building Maintenance Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $35,500.00 Closing: 9/28/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Skilled Tradesman is responsible for the work activities in one or more of the following skilled trades; HVAC (Heating, Ventilation, and Air Conditioning), Plumbing, Electrical, Carpentry, and Mechanical. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Adhere to the vision and guiding principles of the Finance and Administration Division Attend team meetings, open forum meetings, assigned training, and any meetings the skilled trade's foreman instructs. Ensure tools and materials needed to perform daily work assignments are accounted for and in good working order. Perform minor plumbing, electrical, hvac & carpentry general maintenance. Perform work assignments in a professional and courteous manner. Employees shall adhere to all Federal, State and Local codes and regulations governing safety and Code regulations and report all incidents to the skilled trade's team leader. Ensure that all time cards, work orders, and other assigned paper work are correct and turned in on time. Ensure that FAMIS work bench is kept currant and all work descriptions are noted on the work order task list. Contact customers and provide information and schedules for ongoing work if possible or provide courtesy tag when customer is not available. Employees will wear daily the assigned uniform as designated in the Uniform FMOP. Work in a team environment and be able to do minor plumbing, HVAC, electrical and carpentry repairs A strong background in the plumbing or HVAC field is preferred, but not a requirement Assist Facilities Management, whenever needed, on the inclement weather program. Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of the methods, practices, and safety precautions in one or more of the skilled trades, the accepted practices, processes, materials, and tools of the various skilled trades, and the laws and regulations relating to one or more of the skilled trades Ability to provide mathematical and analytical skills necessary to do material estimates for one or more of the skilled trades, read and interpret blueprints, manuals, schematics, building plans, and/or work drawings, understand verbal and written instructions, and maintain inventory on needed parts and tools for one or more of the skilled trades General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 7:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date This position is considered Essential Personnel in Facilities Management Preferred to have a valid Driver's License Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a High School Diploma plus five (5) years of experience as a carpenter or painter as well as completion of required education or training along with the required license or certification in one (1) or more of the following skilled trades listed below: Must be licensed as a Journeyman Electrician in accordance with ACA 17-28-304, Journeyman Plumber in accordance with ACA 17-38-301 or HVAC Mechanics in accordance with ACA 17-33-301 Additional requirements determined by the agency for recruiting purposes require review and approval by the Arkansas Department of Higher Education Other job related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the Qualifications Review Committee E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39830": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Skilled Trades Supervisor Working Title Skilled Trades Supervisor Position # A00637 Department Building Maintenance Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $38,500.00 Closing: 9/28/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Skilled Trades Supervisor is responsible for overseeing the skilled tradesman in one or more of the following skilled trades: HVAC (Heating, Ventilation, and Air Conditioning), plumbing, electrical, carpentry, or mechanical. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Adhere to the vision and guiding principles of the Finance and Administration Division Conduct daily team meetings to insure all team members have work assignments and communicate any issues to the skilled trades Forman Ensure team members have tools and materials needed to perform daily work assignments Check status of work in progress, make inspections of completed work and report to the skilled trades' foreman Team leaders shall adhere to all Federal, State and Local codes and regulations governing safety and Code regulations and report all incidents to the skilled trade's foreman Ensure that all team members' time cards, work orders, and other assigned paper work are correct and turned in on time Ensure that team members work benches in FAMIS are currant and proper information is entered into the work order task list Team leaders will wear daily the assigned uniform as designated in the Uniform FMOP. Exceptions will be in writing for approval by the AVC Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of policy and procedures, laws, and regulations relating to one or more of the skilled trades, licensure and certification required for one or more of the skilled trades, the methods, practices, and safety precautions in one or more of the skilled trades, the standard practices, processes, materials, and equipment used in the maintenance and repair of buildings and equipment, and materials, methods, and tools involved in the maintenance, repair, and/or construction of buildings or other structures Ability to calculate time, materials, and labor needed for projects, read and interpret blueprints, manuals, schematics, building plans, and drawings for one or more of the skilled trades, and communicate information and ideas in various environments General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date This position is considered Essential Personnel in Facilities Management Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a High School Diploma Completion of required education or training along with the required license or certification in the following skilled trades: Journeyman Electrician according to ACA 17-28-304, Journeyman Plumber according to ACA 17-38-301, and HVAC Mechanics according to ACA 17-33-301; plus one year of experience, including six months in a leadership capacity Six (6) years of experience, including one (1) year in a leadership capacity Preferred to posses a valid Driver's License Other job related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the qualifications review committee E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39835": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Temporary Instructor 9 Mo Working Title Temporary Instructor of Special Education Position # F00642 Department School of Teacher Education Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/17/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Educational Leadership, Curriculum and Special Education (ELCSE) of the College of Education and Behavioral Science is seeking applicants for a 9-month, non-tenure track Temporary Instructor of Special Education position. Candidates will teach in an online Special Education Program, which may include initial and advanced programs in special education K-12. The successful candidate will be a strong collaborator and have a desire to connect with colleagues and build relationships to ensure a strong program. The successful candidate will have experience in developing and teaching special education and curriculum courses, mentoring students, and being involved in appropriate activities for the maintenance and continuous improvement of the program. Candidates are expected to be well-versed in behavior management, characteristics of exceptional learners, special education law and ethics, educational assessment, the Science of Reading, and experience in supervising field activities Duties & Responsibilities: Instruction and course development in special education. Teach 15 hours in special education and/or a variety of areas at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Develop and modify courses as needed Work with a team of academic assistants to support the courses the candidate designs Work collaboratively with faculty in the special education program and other department programs Provide supervision for field experiences Serve on program, department, and university committees Participate in program, department, college, and university-level meetings Carry out other functions as may be appropriate to the position Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: • Candidates will preferably demonstrate successful teaching experience at the master's and specialist levels; have experience with online teaching, Canvas LMS, and be proficient in utilizing and incorporating technology into instruction and research efforts. • Knowledge/experience regarding literacy and assessment (specifically Science of Reading, and the use of High-Quality Instructional Materials). General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Preferred Qualifications: • Classroom teaching experience (a minimum of three years) in P-12 public schools in Special Education • Teaching experience in higher education • Teaching experience in on-line teaching Minimum Qualifications: An earned Master's degree in Special Education or in a related field of education E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    }
  },
